---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Methodology">
  <style>
    .page{ max-width:680px; margin:0 auto; padding:90px 32px 110px; }
    .eyebrow{
      font-family:'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size:11px;
      letter-spacing:.16em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--cyan);
      margin-bottom:16px; display:block;
    }
    .page h1{
      font-family:'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-weight:700;
      font-size:clamp(28px,4.6vw,40px); line-height:1.15; letter-spacing:-.01em;
      margin-bottom:36px;
    }
    .page h2{
      font-family:'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size:13px; letter-spacing:.1em;
      text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--oxblood); margin:44px 0 16px;
    }
    .page h2:first-of-type{ margin-top:0; }
    .page p{ font-size:18px; line-height:1.75; color:var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom:20px; }
    .page p strong{ color:var(--paper); font-weight:600; }
    .page code{ font-family:'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size:0.85em; background:rgba(184,57,75,0.08); padding:1px 5px; color:var(--paper); }

    .scale{ border:1px solid var(--redact-border); margin:28px 0; }
    .scale-row{
      display:grid; grid-template-columns:80px 1fr; gap:16px;
      padding:16px 20px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--redact-border);
      font-size:16px; align-items:baseline;
    }
    .scale-row:last-child{ border-bottom:none; }
    .scale-row span:last-child{ color:var(--text-secondary); }

    .badge{
      display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:6px;
      font-family:'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size:11px; letter-spacing:.06em;
      text-transform:uppercase; padding:4px 8px; border:1px solid currentColor;
      width:fit-content;
    }
    .badge-dot{ width:6px; height:6px; border-radius:50%; background:currentColor; }
    .badge.low{ color:var(--cyan); }
    .badge.medium{ color:var(--amber); }
    .badge.high{ color:var(--oxblood); }

    .contact-note{
      font-family:'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted);
      border-top:1px solid var(--redact-border); padding-top:24px; margin-top:50px;
    }
    .contact-note a{ color:var(--cyan); text-decoration:none; }
    .contact-note a:hover{ text-decoration:underline; }
  </style>

  <div class="page">
    <span class="eyebrow">Methodology</span>
    <h1>How a case file gets filed.</h1>

    <h2>Sourcing</h2>
    <p>Cases come from three places: security disclosures already made public but never widely reported, first-hand findings from engineers who reach out to us directly, and our own testing against open-source RAG frameworks and reference architectures. <strong>We do not test production systems we don't have permission to test.</strong></p>

    <h2>Verification</h2>
    <p>Before a case is filed, we reproduce it — either directly, or against a minimal environment that mirrors the reported configuration. If we can't reproduce a finding, it doesn't get published as a confirmed case; it stays in the backlog until it can be verified or ruled out.</p>

    <h2>Severity Rating</h2>
    <p>Every case is rated on what it exposes and how easily, not on how alarming it sounds.</p>
    <div class="scale">
      <div class="scale-row">
        <span class="badge low"><span class="badge-dot"></span>Low</span>
        <span>Requires unusual configuration or privileged access to trigger; limited or non-sensitive data exposed.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="scale-row">
        <span class="badge medium"><span class="badge-dot"></span>Medium</span>
        <span>Exploitable under common configurations; exposes internal but not highly sensitive data.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="scale-row">
        <span class="badge high"><span class="badge-dot"></span>High</span>
        <span>Exploitable under default or widely-deployed configurations; exposes sensitive, private, or cross-tenant data.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Disclosure</h2>
    <p>Where a case involves a specific vendor or open-source project, we notify the maintainers before publication and give them a chance to respond, patch, or comment. A case is marked <strong>disclosed</strong> once that window has passed, regardless of whether a fix shipped.</p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>If a filed case turns out to be wrong, outdated, or resolved, we update it in place and note the change with a date — we don't quietly edit history.</p>

    <h2>API</h2>
    <p>Every case is available as free, public JSON — no key, no signup required. Useful for feeding a Slack bot, a security dashboard, or your own tooling.</p>
    <div class="scale">
      <div class="scale-row">
        <span class="badge low">GET</span>
        <span><code>/api/cases.json</code> — all cases, newest first</span>
      </div>
      <div class="scale-row">
        <span class="badge low">GET</span>
        <span><code>/api/cases/:caseId.json</code> — one case, full detail (e.g. <code>/api/cases/025.json</code>)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="scale-row">
        <span class="badge low">GET</span>
        <span><code>/api/latest.json</code> — most recent 5 cases, lightweight</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>Want the latest cases on your own site? Drop this in:</p>
    <pre style="background:var(--redact);border:1px solid var(--redact-border);color:var(--cyan);font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:13px;padding:16px 18px;overflow-x:auto;margin:20px 0 30px;">&lt;div id="ragbleed-widget"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;script src="https://ragbleed.com/widget.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</pre>

    <div class="contact-note">Have a finding to report, or something to correct? <a href="mailto:tips@ragbleed.com">tips@ragbleed.com</a></div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
